 120: 
 121: ### 3.1 Degenerate cases: f₀ ≤ 40 without certificates
 122: 
 123: Vertices of a hull of a union are vertices of a part, so
 124: f₀(Q) ≤ f₀(Z^a) + f₀(Z^b). A 3-dimensional zonotope's vertex count
 125: equals the chamber count of the central arrangement of its generators'
 126: normal planes; five planes give at most 2(C(4,0)+C(4,1)+C(4,2)) = 22
 127: chambers, attained only when the arrangement is simple. Hence:
 128: 
 129: - if U is **non-generic** (a vanishing determinant, a repeated or
 130:   antiparallel direction, a zero direction — anything making the
 131:   arrangement non-simple or smaller), each copy has ≤ 20 vertices and
 132:   f₀(Q) ≤ 40;
