 137: Both are < 42, so from here on U is generic and both copies have full
 138: support.
 139: 
 140: ### 3.2 Instance normalization: WLOG χ(U) = χ_ref and s ∈ four subsets
 141: 
 142: The group G = S₅ ⋉ {±1}⁵ acts on configurations by
 143: (π, ε)·U = (ε_i·u_{π⁻¹(i)})ᵢ. This action **preserves the polytope and
 144: f₀ exactly**: reorientation u_i ↦ −u_i fixes each segment
 145: m_i + w_i[−u_i, u_i] as a set, and relabeling permutes the segments
 146: (with midpoints, weights, and split entries carried along, s ↦ π·s). On
 147: chirotopes it acts by χ ↦ (π,ε)·χ as implemented in
 148: `check_split_orbits.py`.
 149: 
 150: Two exact computations:
 151: 
 152: - **Single orbit** (`../check_om35_uniqueness.py`, stdlib): the uniform
 153:   rank-3 chirotopes on 5 elements number exactly 384 and form a single
 154:   G-orbit containing χ_ref. So every generic instance can be moved by
 155:   some g ∈ G — without changing its polytope — to an instance whose
 156:   configuration has chirotope exactly χ_ref.
 157: - **Split orbits** (`check_split_orbits.py`, stdlib, exit 0): the
 158:   stabilizer of χ_ref has order 10 with faithful permutation image (the
 159:   pentagon group D₅). Its orbits on split subsets are: {∅}; all five
 160:   1-subsets; two orbits of 2-subsets, represented by {0,1} and {0,2};
 161:   and the complementary structure for k ≥ 3. Having landed at χ_ref, a
 162:   further stabilizer element (which fixes χ_ref, hence keeps the
 163:   configuration realizing χ_ref) normalizes the split subset to one of
 164:   **∅, {0}, {0,1}, {0,2}** or a complement of one of these.
 165: 
 166: Complements reduce to the four representatives by the **global flip**:
 167: swapping the roles of the two copies maps (σ, s) ↦ (flip σ, −s) where
 168: flip negates σ and swaps the two rays of each class, and
 169: Row(flip σ, −s; class, ray) = Row(σ, s; class, −ray) — an exact row
 170: correspondence, so certificates transport by the same ray swap
 171: (verified exactly on samples: `check_transport.py`, "FLIP OK").
 172: Geometrically: swapping the copies negates the support-function
 173: difference, i.e. (T, s) ↦ (−T, −s), which exchanges the positive and
 174: negative extreme rays of each facet normal — whence the ray swap.
 175: 
 176: ### 3.3 Certificate transport
 177: 
 178: Let g = (π, ε) fix χ_ref (a stabilizer element used in §3.2's split
 179: normalization) or, more generally, map the instance's chirotope to
 180: χ_ref. The labeled system transforms covariantly:
 181: 
 182: - C_{lo,hi}(g·U) = τ·C_{ij}(U) with τ = ±ε_lo·ε_hi (sign − iff π
