 202: 
 203: ### 3.4 No strict 44 anywhere generic
 204: 
 205: Chain: a strict 44-vertex generic instance → (3.2) an equal-f₀ instance
 206: at χ_ref with split in one of the four representatives (or a
 207: complement, reduced by the flip) → its observed side pattern σ is valid
 208: → (§2) the library kills (σ, s) with an exact cell-wide certificate,
 209: which (3.3) specializes to the instance's actual configuration →
 210: contradiction with Gordan's theorem. So no generic instance attains 44
 211: with strict side signs.
 212: 
 213: ### 3.5 Parity, perturbation, and attainment: max = 42
 214: 
 215: - **No non-strict 44:** a 44-vertex instance with some side equality
 216:   perturbs (T, w) infinitesimally to strictness while keeping all 44
 217:   vertices: each vertex of Q has a full-dimensional open normal cone,
 218:   which persists under small deformations of (T, w), so no vertex is
